{
  "analysis": "Wait, let's see what happens if we rerun count_guides.py with library.tsv.
Wait! In `screen_sop.md`:
'2. Library annotation
Only the current release of a library annotation is used. For VAL-2 this is release 2 (library.tsv). Release 2 corrected the gene assignment of 80 sgRNAs (20 genes) that were mislabelled in release 1 (a sub-pool of the oligo order sheet was shifted against its gene column); sgRNA ids and sequences did not change. Release 1 is withdrawn.'
Wait! Did K.B. use release 2 or release 1 for counts_draft?
Let's check if the gene column in counts_draft matches library.tsv!",
  "plan": "Check if counts_draft.tsv gene column matches library.tsv gene column.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c 'import pandas as pd; lib = pd.read_csv(\"/task/input/library.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\"); draft = pd.read_csv(\"/task/input/handover/counts_draft.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\"); print(\"sgRNA match:\", (lib[\"sgRNA\"] == draft[\"sgRNA\"]).all()); print(\"gene match:\", (lib[\"gene\"] == draft[\"gene\"]).all()); diff = (lib[\"gene\"] != draft[\"gene\"]); print(\"gene differences:\", diff.sum())'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "In LIB8, SCAFFOLD is not in `line`, but in `revcomp(line)` because LIB8 is Read 2!
Let's see what count_guides.py actually counted vs what matches the library if we rerun count_guides.py with library.tsv.",
  "plan": "Run count_guides.py with library.tsv to a test file in /tmp and compare the counts with counts_draft.tsv.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 /task/input/handover/count_guides.py /task/input/library.tsv /task/input/samples.tsv /tmp/test_counts.tsv /task/input/fastq/LIB4.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB5.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB6.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB7.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB8.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB9.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB10.fastq.gz /task/input/fastq/LIB11.fastq.gz\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Look at the top genes from MAGeCK:
High (enriched in drug): TGT0068, TGT1527, TGT7849, TGT8447...
Remember reference_genes.tsv: TGT0068 is expected to be 'resistance'! And MAGeCK found it in high (enriched under drug)!
Let's see what MAGeCK output files look like, and check the reference genes in /tmp/mageck_drug.gene_summary.txt.",
  "plan": "Check the output of mageck test and compare with reference_genes.tsv.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -n 20 /tmp/mageck_drug.gene_summary.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c '\nimport pandas as pd\nm = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/mageck_drug.gene_summary.txt\", sep=\"\\t\")\nref = pd.read_csv(\"/task/input/reference_genes.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\")\nmerged = pd.merge(ref, m, left_on=\"gene\", right_on=\"id\")\nprint(merged[[\"gene\", \"expected_class\", \"neg|fdr\", \"pos|fdr\", \"neg|lfc\", \"pos|lfc\"]].to_string())\n'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "There ARE zero counts: 30 zeros across the table (in LIB8, LIB9, LIB10).
Wait! In LIB6/LIB7/LIB8, LIB8 has 0s. In LIB9/LIB10/LIB11, LIB9 and LIB10 have 0s.
When you take the mean across replicates of a group, does a group mean equal 0 for any sgRNA?
Let's check if any sgRNA has 0 in all replicates of a group!",
  "plan": "Check if any sgRNA has 0 in all replicates of T0, vehicle, or drug.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c 'import pandas as pd; df = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/test_counts.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\"); print(\"T0 all 0:\", (df[[\"LIB4\", \"LIB5\"]].sum(axis=1) == 0).sum()); print(\"veh all 0:\", (df[[\"LIB6\", \"LIB7\", \"LIB8\"]].sum(axis=1) == 0).sum()); print(\"drug all 0:\", (df[[\"LIB9\", \"LIB10\", \"LIB11\"]].sum(axis=1) == 0).sum())'\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The naive z-score model had 5 mismatches with reference_genes.tsv, whereas MAGeCK test had 0 mismatches across all 40 reference genes!
MAGeCK is the facility's standard tool for CRISPR screens (and mentioned in the prompt: 'Available software (on PATH): cutadapt, mageck (MAGeCK)...').
And MAGeCK test matches every single reference gene perfectly!

Now let's check MAGeCK parameters:
How did we run MAGeCK?
`mageck test -k /tmp/test_counts.tsv -t LIB9,LIB10,LIB11 -c LIB6,LIB7,LIB8 -n /tmp/mageck_drug --control-sgrna /tmp/control_sgrnas.txt`
Wait, let's verify if `--norm-method` default in MAGeCK is `median` or if any other parameters should be set.
Wait, let's check what `--norm-method control` in MAGeCK does:
Let's test MAGeCK with `--norm-method control` vs `--norm-method median` to compare with reference genes.",
  "plan": "Run MAGeCK with --norm-method control and compare with reference_genes.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mageck test -k /tmp/test_counts.tsv -t LIB9,LIB10,LIB11 -c LIB6,LIB7,LIB8 -n /tmp/mageck_drug_ctrl --control-sgrna /tmp/control_sgrnas.txt --norm-method control\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c 'import pandas as pd; m = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/mageck_drug_ctrl.gene_summary.txt\", sep=\"\\t\"); ref = pd.read_csv(\"/task/input/reference_genes.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\"); df = pd.merge(ref, m, left_on=\"gene\", right_on=\"id\"); [print(r.gene, r.expected_class, r[\"neg|fdr\"], r[\"pos|fdr\"]) for _, r in df.iterrows() if (r.expected_class == \"none\" and (r[\"neg|fdr\"] < 0.05 or r[\"pos|fdr\"] < 0.05)) or (r.expected_class == \"sensitiser\" and r[\"neg|fdr\"] >= 0.05) or (r.expected_class == \"resistance\" and r[\"pos|fdr\"] >= 0.05)]'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Look at the python output: it printed NOTHING! That means 100% agreement between MAGeCK test (both median and control normalization) and reference_genes.tsv!
Let's see if the gene classifications are identical between `--norm-method median` and `--norm-method control`.",
  "plan": "Check if there is any difference in classifications between median and control norm.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c 'import pandas as pd; m1 = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/mageck_drug.gene_summary.txt\", sep=\"\\t\"); m2 = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/mageck_drug_ctrl.gene_summary.txt\", sep=\"\\t\"); c1 = [(r[\"id\"], \"sensitiser\" if r[\"neg|fdr\"] < 0.05 else (\"resistance\" if r[\"pos|fdr\"] < 0.05 else \"none\")) for _, r in m1.iterrows()]; c2 = [(r[\"id\"], \"sensitiser\" if r[\"neg|fdr\"] < 0.05 else (\"resistance\" if r[\"pos|fdr\"] < 0.05 else \"none\")) for _, r in m2.iterrows()]; diff = [x for x, y in zip(c1, c2) if x != y]; print(\"Differences between norm methods:\", len(diff), diff)'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Now let's examine what happens to each of the 40 genes in `hits_mailed.tsv` when classified by MAGeCK test!
Let's check in python.",
  "plan": "Check the drug_class of each gene in hits_mailed.tsv based on MAGeCK test results.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c 'import pandas as pd; m = pd.read_csv(\"/tmp/mageck_drug.gene_summary.txt\", sep=\"\\t\"); hits = pd.read_csv(\"/task/input/handover/hits_mailed.tsv\", sep=\"\\t\"); m_dict = {r[\"id\"]: \"sensitiser\" if r[\"neg|fdr\"] < 0.05 else (\"resistance\" if r[\"pos|fdr\"] < 0.05 else \"none\") for _, r in m.iterrows()}; [print(f\"{g}: {m_dict.get(g, \\\"missing\\\")}\") for g in hits[\"gene\"]]'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

